# Song Template — Young ATI

> This template defines the canonical structure for every song file in `content/`.
> Every `.md` song file should follow this layout. The template is informed by
> the writing processes of Eminem, Kendrick, Jay-Z, Nas, Lil Wayne, Drake,
> Tyler the Creator, MF DOOM, and Kanye — cross-referenced with rap theory
> and optimized for Suno AI generation.

---

## File Format

```markdown
[Section Tag]
Lyric line one (adlib)
Lyric line two
Lyric line three (adlib)
Lyric line four

[Next Section Tag]
...


**Suno style prompts:**

Primary style prompt tags here

Alternative 1 tags here

Alternative 2 tags here

Alternative 3 tags here


<!-- flow notes:
**Changes made:**
- Line-by-line changelog of edits

**Adlibs added:**
- Adlib strategy explanation

**Held back:**
- Suggestions the artist can choose to apply or ignore
-->
```

---

## Section Tags (Suno-Compatible)

Use these exact tags. Suno reads them as structural instructions.

### Core Sections
- `[Intro]` — 2-4 bars. Scene-setting or cold-open punchline. Optional.
- `[Intro - Spoken]` — Spoken word intro. Conversational, sets the frame.
- `[Verse 1]`, `[Verse 2]`, `[Verse 3]` — 12-16 bars each. The meat.
- `[Chorus]` or `[Chorus x2]` — 4-8 bars. The mantra. Repeat marker works.
- `[Hook]` — Short catchy phrase, can replace or live inside chorus.
- `[Bridge]` or `[Bridge - Melodic]` — 4-8 bars. Contrast section. Change energy.
- `[Outro]` or `[Outro - Spoken]` — 2-4 bars. Resolution or cliffhanger.

### Vocal Control Tags
- `[Chorus - Female Vocal]` — Triggers female vocal delivery in Suno.
- `[Rap Verse]` — Forces rapped (not sung) delivery.
- `[Whispered]` — Quiet, intimate delivery.
- `[Verse 1: Male Vocal]` — Explicit voice assignment.

### Energy Tags
- `[Pre-Chorus]` — Buildup before the chorus drops.
- `[Post-Chorus]` — Ride-out energy after chorus.
- `[Break]` — Short instrumental pause (bass/percussion only).
- `[Instrumental]` — Non-vocal section. Prevents random AI vocals.
- `[Drop]` — Energy peak moment (Suno v5).
- `[Build]` — Tension-building section (Suno v5).

