## Flow & Cadence

### The Pocket
Match your syllable density to the beat:
- **Quarter notes** (1 syllable/beat) — slow, heavy, deliberate
- **Eighth notes** (2 syllables/beat) — standard rap cadence
- **Sixteenth notes** (4 syllables/beat) — double-time, rapid-fire
- **Triplets** (3 syllables/beat) — bouncy trap feel

### Variation is Everything
- Change flow every 4-8 bars to prevent listener fatigue
- Alternate dense bars (14+ syllables) with short punchy bars (6-8)
- Push ahead of the beat for urgency, fall behind for laid-back feel
- Use pauses as rhythmic tools — silence hits harder than words sometimes

### Melodic Moments (Young ATI Signature)
Extended vowels signal sing-rap delivery:
- `loooooow`, `fuuuun`, `craaazy`, `heeeeell`
- Suno actually stretches the note on extended vowels
- Use on emotional peaks or chorus lines
- 1-2 per verse max, more in hooks

