## Adlibs

Adlibs go in parentheses at the END of lines. Suno treats `()` as background/secondary vocals.

### Energy Levels
| Type | Examples | When |
|------|----------|------|
| Hype | (woo!), (sheesh), (let's go) | After flex bars, energy peaks |
| Reaction | (damn), (wow), (god damn) | After hard punchlines |
| Texture | (uh), (yeah), (nah) | Fill rhythmic gaps, add bounce |
| Sound FX | (skrrt), (brr), (pow), (beep boop) | Momentum shifts, metaphor emphasis |
| Echo | Repeat last word: "ghost (ghost)" | Emphasize key words |
| Soft | (no love), (why though?) | Vulnerable moments, chorus |

### Rules
- ~40-60% of bars get adlibs. Not every line.
- Never interrupt the bar — adlibs go at the end.
- Match energy: hard bars → hard adlibs, vulnerable bars → soft or none.
- Don't repeat the same adlib more than twice per song.
- Chorus gets minimal adlibs — keep it clean for repetition.

